{
  "box": "gh#39 follow-up assertions A-D: closed-dialog inertness on all 9 PlayerSetup pages, post-dismiss coordinate inertness, at-top/at-bottom anchoring at the innerHeight/2 class boundary, and modified-click pass-through. Full wording in \"purpose\".",
  "method": "scripts/leave-confirm-probe.mjs via scripts/driver.mjs against dist/ served at :4321. Viewports 320x900 for A/B/D, 320x356 per-page for C’s real tap, 320x900 for C’s anchoring check. Detector calibrated red on 3 unfixed builds — see \"detectorCalibration\".",
  "capturedAtCommit": "1c84799",
  "capturedAtCommitNote": "Backfilled 2026-08-18 at 9510d21 — these five keys were NOT written by the probe run. The capture base is derived from git, not recorded at run time: a0c360b added this file together with scripts/leave-confirm-probe.mjs and scripts/crawl-check-gamenav.mjs and changed no src/, so the run used uncommitted probe scripts against its parent 1c84799 (the leave-confirm guard itself). Tree was dirty at capture. Git can show only what was committed alongside in a0c360b (docs/verification/evidence/39/*.json and scripts/{crawl-check-gamenav,driver,gamenav-again-grid-probe,leave-confirm-probe,no-nav-in-stage-probe}.mjs); a change made and discarded before that commit would leave no trace, and run-time HEAD is assumed, not proven, to equal a0c360b's parent. The pre-fix half ran against a guard-absent tree (1c84799~1 = 78af47b, or a reverted working tree); the artifacts do not distinguish the two, so no sha is claimed for it.",
  "verdict": "PROVEN",
  "purpose": "gh#39 follow-up. Four assertions the original six-step verify never made, each confirmed RED on the shipped guard before the fix and green after it. A. a CLOSED <dialog id=\"leave-confirm\"> must generate no boxes and answer no elementFromPoint, on all 9 pages that render PlayerSetup. B. after the guard is dismissed with the safe branch, no coordinate it occupied may navigate, and pendingHref must be clear. C. the at-top/at-bottom anchoring must survive a tap AT the class boundary (innerHeight / 2), the coordinate the shipped 215px figure never tested. D. a cmd/ctrl/shift/middle click must reach the browser untouched, because opening a sibling game in a second tab is the round-PRESERVING gesture.",
  "probe": "scripts/leave-confirm-probe.mjs (run via scripts/driver.mjs, dist/ served at :4321, 320px wide)",
  "detectorCalibration": "A: the grid scan that must find nothing while the dialog is closed must find its buttons while it is open, one pass per page, in that order — see detectorPerPage, every page reports buttonHitsWhileOpen > 0. D: the plain click on the same link must still be intercepted in the same pass, or a \"not intercepted\" result would only mean the guard was off. C: the run asserts the tap actually landed on the link (coversBoundary) instead of assuming the scroll worked; a miss reads VOID, not PASS.",
  "viewports": {
    "assertionsAandBandD": "320x900",
    "assertionC_realTap": "320x356, solved per page rather than guessed. GameNav sits near the document end with only the footer below it, so scrollIntoView clamps at max scroll and the link stops a fixed K px above the viewport bottom; H = 2K is the one height where max scroll puts a link exactly on the split. At 900 no non-exempt link reaches y=450 at all, which is why the shipped verify never tested that coordinate.",
    "assertionC_anchoringAt900": "320x900 with the class set directly — a CSS-placement question, not a tap, and the same viewport the 215px figure in 03-double-tap-postfix.json was taken at."
  },
